+# Browser Sync Specifications
+
+## Subscription Lifecycle
+
+- [ ] **BROWSER-001**: On initial load, the system shall transition from disconnected → connecting → subscribed via welcome message with full board snapshot.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-002**: On reconnect after disconnect, the system shall transition disconnected → connecting → catching_up (via catchup batch) → subscribed.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-003**: On network interruption during subscribed state, the system shall auto-reconnect: subscribed → connecting → catching_up → subscribed.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-004**: On authentication expiration (error code auth_expired), the system shall transition to failed state and require user sign-in.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-005**: The system shall track last_applied_revision as the highest revision_id successfully applied to local board state.
+
+## Reconnect Strategy
+
+- [ ] **BROWSER-006**: On clean close or network error, the system shall attempt immediate retry after 500ms.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-007**: On repeated failures, the system shall use exponential backoff: 500ms, 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s, 30s (capped at 30s).
+- [ ] **BROWSER-008**: The system shall apply ±100ms jitter per retry attempt.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-009**: The system shall continue retry attempts for up to 20 minutes; after 20 minutes, transition to failed state requiring user action.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-010**: On reconnect, the system shall send subscribe with last_revision = last_applied_revision.
+
+## Catch-Up Processing
+
+- [ ] **BROWSER-011**: When a catchup batch arrives, the system shall sort revisions by revision_id ascending before applying.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-012**: The system shall apply each revision's operations to local board state in order.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-013**: After applying each revision, the system shall update last_applied_revision and send ack.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-014**: If a revision fails to apply (e.g., unknown stall_id), the system shall log error, skip the revision, continue processing, and surface a warning to the user.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-015**: On catch-up batch completion, the system shall transition to subscribed state.
+
+## Connectivity Indicator
+
+- [ ] **BROWSER-016**: While in subscribed state, the UI shall display a green "Live" indicator.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-017**: While in catching_up state, the UI shall display a yellow "Catching up…" indicator.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-018**: While in connecting state, the UI shall display a yellow "Reconnecting…" indicator.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-019**: While in disconnected state (during retry backoff), the UI shall display a red "Disconnected" indicator with retry countdown.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-020**: While in failed state, the UI shall display a red "Connection failed — sign in to retry" banner.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-021**: Indicator updates shall be synchronous with state transitions (no debounce).
+
+## Revision Application
+
+- [ ] **BROWSER-022**: The system shall support stall_status operations (stall_id, status: open|closed|late|power_issue).
+- [ ] **BROWSER-023**: The system shall support stall_note operations (stall_id, note).
+- [ ] **BROWSER-024**: The system shall support board_note operations (note).
+- [ ] **BROWSER-025**: Revision application shall be synchronous and idempotent per revision (applying same revision twice produces same board state).
+- [ ] **BROWSER-026**: The system shall track last_applied_revision to ensure idempotency across reconnects.
+
+## Edit Command Gating
+
+- [ ] **BROWSER-027**: While in disconnected, connecting, or catching_up state, the UI shall disable edit command submission.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-028**: Edit commands shall only be enabled in subscribed state.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives (for reference)
+
+- [ ] **BROWSER-029**: Reconnect shall use exponential backoff with 30s cap and 20-min max duration.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-030**: Catch-up shall use per-revision ack (not batch ack).
+- [ ] **BROWSER-031**: Connectivity indicator shall be synchronous with no debounce.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-032**: Revision application shall be synchronous and in-order.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-033**: Max catch-up batch size shall align with change store cursor query limit (100 revisions).
