+# Change Store Specifications
+
+## Revision Model
+
+- [ ] **CHANGE-001**: When a command handler commits an edit for an event, the system shall append exactly one revision to that event's revision history with a monotonically increasing revision_id.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-002**: The system shall assign each revision a timestamp of commitment in UTC.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-003**: The system shall record the authorized actor_id on each revision.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-004**: The system shall store the array of atomic board operations for each revision.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-005**: Once committed, a revision shall be immutable.
+
+## Read Indexes
+
+- [ ] **CHANGE-006**: When a browser requests the latest revision for an event, the system shall return the maximum revision_id for that event.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-007**: When a browser requests revisions after a given cursor (last_revision), the system shall return revisions in ascending revision_id order with no gaps, up to the configured batch limit (default 100).
+- [ ] **CHANGE-008**: If the requested cursor exceeds the latest revision, the system shall return an empty result.
+
+## Publication Outbox
+
+- [ ] **CHANGE-009**: When a revision is committed, the system shall write an outbox entry in the same database transaction containing event_id, revision_id, and created_at.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-010**: The system shall assign each outbox entry a monotonically increasing global outbox_id.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-011**: The delivery component shall read outbox entries in outbox_id order.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-012**: When delivery successfully fans out a revision to all subscribed sessions, the system shall mark the outbox entry with published_at.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-013**: Unpublished outbox entries shall be retried on delivery restart.
+
+## Retention
+
+- [ ] **CHANGE-014**: For active events (during published event hours), the system shall retain all revisions.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-015**: For completed events, the system shall retain revisions for 7 days after event close, then archive.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-016**: Published outbox entries shall be retained for 24 hours after published_at, then garbage-collected.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives (for reference)
+
+- [ ] **CHANGE-017**: The system shall use per-event monotonically increasing revision IDs (not global UUIDs or global sequence).
+- [ ] **CHANGE-018**: The system shall use a transactional outbox in the same database (not a separate message queue).
+- [ ] **CHANGE-019**: The default cursor query batch limit shall be 100 revisions per response.
