+# Delivery Specifications
+
+## Session Management
+
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-001**: When a browser opens a WebSocket connection, the system shall authenticate the session via session cookie or token and assign a session_id.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-002**: When an authenticated session sends a subscribe message with event_id, the system shall register the session for that event_id.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-003**: The system shall track last_ack_revision per session for catch-up support.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-004**: When a session disconnects, the system shall remove it from the session registry.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-005**: The system shall support 800 simultaneous WebSocket sessions on a single instance.
+
+## Protocol — Server Messages
+
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-006**: On successful subscribe, the system shall send a welcome message containing session_id, event_id, current_revision, and the full board snapshot.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-007**: When a new revision is published for an event, the system shall fan out a revision message to all sessions subscribed to that event_id.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-008**: When a browser subscribes with a last_revision older than current, the system shall send a catchup message containing the ordered batch of revisions from last_revision+1 to current_revision.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-009**: The system shall send a ping message every 15 seconds to each connected session.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-010**: If a session fails to respond with pong within 10 seconds of a ping, the system shall close the connection.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-011**: On protocol or authentication error, the system shall send an error message with code, message, and retryable flag.
+
+## Protocol — Client Messages
+
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-012**: When the system receives a subscribe message, it shall validate the event_id and optional last_revision.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-013**: When the system receives a ping message, it shall respond with pong containing the client timestamp and server_time.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-014**: When the system receives an ack message with revision_id, it shall update the session's last_ack_revision.
+
+## Outbox Consumption
+
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-015**: The system shall poll the change store outbox for unpublished entries at a 100ms interval.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-016**: For each outbox entry, the system shall load the revision from the change store and fan out to all subscribed sessions.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-017**: The system shall mark an outbox entry published only after successful fan-out to all target sessions.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-018**: If fan-out to a session fails, the system shall retry with exponential backoff; persistent failure shall mark the session for reconnect.
+
+## Fan-Out Behavior
+
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-019**: Fan-out to one slow session shall not block fan-out to other sessions.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-020**: The system shall buffer up to 50 unacknowledged revisions per session; exceeding the buffer shall trigger catch-up on next reconnect.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-021**: On delivery restart, the system shall re-publish any unpublished outbox entries.
+
+## Reconnect Support
+
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-022**: The system shall accept a subscribe message with last_revision and return the appropriate catchup batch from the change store cursor query.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-023**: The session registry shall survive delivery restart (in-memory for pilot; Redis-backed for horizontal scaling).
+
+## Capacity
+
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-024**: The system shall handle opening-time bursts of 20 edits/second (20 fan-outs/second to up to 800 sessions each).
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives (for reference)
+
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-025**: The protocol shall use JSON over WebSocket (not MessagePack or protobuf).
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-026**: Heartbeat interval shall be 15s ping with 10s pong timeout.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-027**: Session registry shall be in-memory for pilot (Redis deferred).
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-028**: Browser shall send explicit ack per revision (not implicit TCP ACK).
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-029**: Outbox consumer shall use 100ms polling interval.
+- [ ] **DELIVERY-030**: Max buffered unacked revisions per session shall be 50.
